#!/bin/sh
# Refuses a seat's commit whose files are ALL documentation.
#
# WHY: on 2026-10-15 15 of 23 commits in a night were docs (plan status, sha corrections, counts). The owner's
# rule is that seats build, fix and improve; an idea or a status goes through the queue, and docs, CHANGELOG
# and TEST-CHANGELOG change ONCE, in the code commit of a finished task. GUIDE rows did not stop the habit.
#
# WHO: only a seat. AGENTHUB_SESSION_NAME is exported to seats and unset on the owner's host, which is how
# prepare-commit-msg tells them apart. The owner, or a seat the owner told to write a document, sets
# OWNER_DOCS_COMMIT=1 for that one commit.
#
# Arguments are the staged files (pre-commit passes them). A commit that touches ANY non-doc file passes.

set -eu

[ -n "${AGENTHUB_SESSION_NAME:-}" ] || exit 0
[ "${OWNER_DOCS_COMMIT:-}" != "1" ] || exit 0
[ "$#" -gt 0 ] || exit 0

for f in "$@"; do
    case "$f" in
        *.md | ai_docs/* | CHANGELOG/* | */CHANGELOG/* | TEST-CHANGELOG.md | NEXT-GEN*) ;;
        *) exit 0 ;;
    esac
done

cat >&2 <<'MSG'
docs-only commit refused: every staged file is documentation.
The owner's rule: seats build, fix and improve. A plan, finding, ruling, status or recount goes through the
queue (one short row), not into a commit. Docs, CHANGELOG and TEST-CHANGELOG change ONCE, in the code commit
of the finished task. Put these files in that commit, or drop them.
Only if the owner asked for this document: OWNER_DOCS_COMMIT=1 git commit ...
MSG
exit 1
